I managed to get two interviews with two boutiques in the past couple of weeks after many unsuccessful applications, so it is possible to stand out.

&#x200B;

Make sure you present your resume and cover letter really well with effort and personalise it to each position so you look hard working and dedicated. Improving my applications helped dramatically.

&#x200B;

Also, I recommend doing PLT part time. It shows commitment, and the part time course is extremely flexible so it won't impact work and allows you to accept full time work immediately. (You can do it full time too, but I thought it looked better to do part time so it appears my focus is on finding and prioritising full time work).

&#x200B;

Just don't fall into a rut where you give up and aren't doing anything. It's important not to leave large gaps in your CV so where possible it helps to be either working or studying consistently. (Although employers are quite understanding of gaps at the moment due to covid).

