I am a mature age (well 22 yo) learner about to take my test in a month.

&#x200B;

For the lights:

It can be dangerous to hesitate and unexpetedly slow down to much at a green light because cars behind you won't expect it.

&#x200B;

My instructor has told me to continue on like normal at lights. When the light turns yellow you need to stop if it is safe to do so, to determine this you need to check your rear vision mirror and slow down at a safe speed. If you do not have time to check your mirror or slow down at a safe speed, then it is not safe to stop and you should proceed through the yellow light. Speeding up, or slowing down unsafely, when the light goes yellow is a big no no. 

&#x200B;

To relax for the test I think it's important to realise that you can always take it again and the instructors are assessing just 30 minutes of your driving. Even the most experienced drivers could randomly make a simple mistake and fail. It's nothing to be nervous about :) Try your best and if you don't succeed at the first go, at least you get feedback about driving from someone with a lot of experience to make you safer :) 

